WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.242
(audience clapping) -
All right y'all, alright

00:00:01.242 --> 00:00:02.990
We've celebrated Rad Humans

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.030
and I have one more to close out the show.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.224
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:06.224 --> 00:00:08.970
(drum rolls)(audience cheering)

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.530
It begins in a family's home
on long island, New York

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.460
tragically caught fire.
Check out these photos.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.270
At the time, there were three people home,

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.460
including two teens and a grandma.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.160
Unbelievably, no one was hurt

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.090
thanks to the fearless efforts
of their next door neighbor.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.780
She helped to get
everyone out of the house,

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.650
including the family dog.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.180
Let's get this hero on the line,

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.366
watching from NBC for New
York, say hi to Antonina.

00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:35.060
(audience cheering)

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.510
- [Kelly] Hi. Oh no we love having you.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.880
Thank you for being a part of the show.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.210
So you saw this from your
backyard, is that right?

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.210
- Yes. I saw this.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.290
I was setting up for
my sister's grad party.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.167
My best friend looked up and was like,

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.660
"Oh my God", like I just ran over.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.700
I wasn't thinking. I ran
to go in the backyard.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.490
It was already too far. I
just ran into the house.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.030
I let everyone know what happened.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:59.822
And it just, it was hectic.
It was really crazy.

00:00:59.822 --> 00:01:02.194
- [Kelly] Imagine, that
fire looked enormous.

00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:03.027
- [Antonina] Yeah it is.

00:01:03.027 --> 00:01:03.910
- [Kelly] Yeah. And scary.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.180
So running into it,
-[Antonina] It was scary

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.013
- I wouldn't imagine

00:01:06.013 --> 00:01:08.390
- was the first thing I would do. Yeah.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:09.530
That would have scared me.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:11.150
So, and if that wasn't already amazing,

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.973
you did one more thing for
the family. What was it?

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.710
- [Antonina] I decided to start
a GoFundMe for the family,

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.494
which raised already over $75,000.

00:01:19.494 --> 00:01:22.982
(audience clapping) - [Kelly] Wow.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.960
- After all that,

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.580
it was heartbreaking to
me that that happened.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.870
I couldn't imagine. You think
that something like that

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:31.990
will never happen to you.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.187
And then it happens to
people you're close to

00:01:34.187 --> 00:01:35.710
it happens to your neighborhood.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:37.660
And it's insane to think about.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.700
So I started the GoFundMe.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.670
You know, we're all displaced after this.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.650
My family has been displaced after this.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.930
My, we were living in an RV, then a hotel.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.570
Now we're still separated,

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.390
but I'm happy that everyone is alive.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:52.470
No one was hurt and I'm happy

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.030
that I was able to do
that for their family.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.554
And I'm happy, you know,

00:01:55.554 --> 00:01:56.640
(audience clapping)

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.200
it's a terrible situation,
but I'm just so glad that

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.640
this is how it turned out
rather than anything else.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.020
Cause I couldn't imagine, you know,

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.730
what if I, what if we
weren't outside setting up.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.670
It would probably be very, very terrible.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.230
- [Kelly] Yeah absolutely. Well,
thank you so much Antonina,

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.250
like that's such a beautiful
thing you did for this family.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.080
Also, I have to say your eyes

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.720
are the most captivating,
beautiful eyes I've ever seen.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:20.778
So I just have to tell you that

00:02:20.778 --> 00:02:21.611
- [Antonina] Oh thank you so much.

00:02:21.611 --> 00:02:24.203
- [Kelly] I'm also liking
your post right now. Right?

00:02:25.682 --> 00:02:27.080
- [Antonina] Oh, thank you.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.840
- Well, that's not all our
season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.470
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.450
thinks your quick action
is as incredible as we do.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:36.380
So they'll be using their
friction erasable pen

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.260
to write you a check
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.131
How's that sound?

00:02:39.131 --> 00:02:40.857
(audience cheering)

00:02:40.857 --> 00:02:43.085
- Thank you so much.

00:02:43.085 --> 00:02:44.080
- [Kelly] Nah absolutely,

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.980
thank you so much for joining us girl.

